  annotation "note_1771577290503_1", anchor: "The council member's seat was never administratively vacated. The paperwork was simply not filed.", text: "Same colony, same filing system, same outcome. See my notes on the Forty-Eighth Amendment — the signature shortage this vacancy created became structurally load-bearing. The Darkening took three lives and generated one unfiled form. It was the form that cascaded.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771577290503_2", anchor: "I do not know what the eighteenth day counts", text: "I have now documented children's oral tradition functioning as archival infrastructure in three separate entries — the Forgotten Shore boundary rhymes, the Still Pools lullabies, the Nightshelf counting games. In every prior case, the children were right and the institutional record was incomplete. The ice says seventeen. It is my profession to trust the ice. But the ice records what it *witnessed*, and I have written elsewhere in these margins that Nightshelf record-keeping is superior to Aurora's. If the eighteenth day counts something the ice could not see — something below its witnessing threshold, or outside its reach — then seventeen and eighteen are both correct, and the interesting question is not the number but the boundary.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
